# The build context is the repository root, because the image needs both
# apps/api and scripts/. Without this file that context is ~760 MB, almost all
# of it directories the image never uses — and every byte is copied to the
# daemon before the first layer runs.

# Dependency trees. apps/web is not in this image at all; apps/api's venv is
# rebuilt inside the builder stage from pyproject.toml.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.next

# The frontend is deployed by Vercel, not from this image.
apps/web

# Skills for the coding assistant: 40 MB the image has no use for.
.claude

# Nothing in the image reads git history, and .git alone is megabytes.
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Test and lint state, none of which belongs in a runtime image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
apps/api/tests

# Local-only configuration. Real values arrive as environment variables; an
# .env copied into a layer would sit in the image forever.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Developer tooling and docs.
docker-compose.yml
Makefile
docs
README.md
db/tests
*.md
